From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: plane samplers can leave the rows of the bars out

A caller that draws a letterboxed 2160-row picture to a target of the same
size, and writes the rows above and below the picture itself in the shader
that writes the target, has no use for what the samplers of the planes
compute for those rows: the chroma planes and the planes of an enhancement
layer are scaled up for all 2160 rows, in two passes each, and a quarter of
that (a 2.39:1 film) is thrown away.

New pl_render_params.active_rows: the rows that hold picture. With it set,
the sampler of a plane of the image or of its enhancement layer returns
black for the other rows without sampling, in the pass that is merged into
the shader of the target and in the intermediate pass of a separable
scaler. The rows that hold picture are sampled as always, and no pass
reads another row than its own from an intermediate texture (the first
pass scales rows, the second one columns), so what is drawn in them does
not change. Default off; the bounds are a uniform, so the text of the
shader does not depend on them.

The sampler that is merged into the shader of the target tells the rows by
gl_FragCoord, with the flip of the target. If libplacebo could not merge
it and drew the plane to a texture first, those would be the coordinates
of another pass. So that this cannot go unnoticed, the caller has to
define PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET in the shader that writes the target, and the
sampler carries a line that only compiles where it is defined: the render
then fails, which the caller sees.

The idea is the "active rows" of the Intel Dolby Vision LibreELEC fork,
CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV, R1.0.0 Beta2 (commit
2e2fc3e954bb808daf3472250c0f7dc3f301fe5f), file
CB1/patches/libplacebo/libplacebo-9912-native-transport.patch, which has
it as a second entry point of the renderer for its own transport. Written
anew here as a parameter, with the check and limited to planes that are
read.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the files changed,
whose notices stay as they are.
---
 src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/renderer.c                    | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

diff --git a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
--- a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
+++ b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
@@ -354,6 +354,24 @@
     // user, but it should be set to false once those values are "dialed in".
     bool dynamic_constants;
 
+    // The rows of a target of 2160 rows that hold picture: from
+    // `active_rows[0]` up to, and not including, `active_rows[1]`, counted
+    // from the top of the picture. Both 0: all of them, the default.
+    //
+    // For a caller that writes every other row of the target itself, in the
+    // shader that writes the target (a hook). The samplers of the planes of
+    // the image and of its enhancement layer then leave those rows out: they
+    // return black for them without sampling, also in the intermediate pass
+    // of a separable scaler, whose target has that height too. The rows that
+    // hold picture are sampled as always.
+    //
+    // A sampler that is part of the shader that writes the target tells the
+    // rows by the coordinates of the target. So that it is known to be in
+    // that shader, the caller has to `#define PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET 1` in it
+    // (the prelude of its hook): anywhere else the sampler does not compile,
+    // and the render fails instead of leaving out other rows.
+    int active_rows[2];
+
     // This callback is invoked for every pass successfully executed in the
     // process of rendering a frame. Optional.
     //
diff --git a/src/renderer.c b/src/renderer.c
--- a/src/renderer.c
+++ b/src/renderer.c
@@ -690,11 +690,59 @@
     return info;
 }
 
+// Leaves the rows outside `pl_render_params.active_rows` out of the sampler of a
+// plane: see the description of that field. `target`: the shader is part of the
+// one that writes the target of the render, whose coordinates may be flipped;
+// otherwise it writes an intermediate texture of its own, which never is.
+static bool skip_inactive_rows(struct pass_state *pass, pl_shader sh, int height,
+                               bool target)
+{
+    const struct pl_render_params *params = pass->params;
+    const int y0 = params->active_rows[0], y1 = params->active_rows[1];
+    if (height != 2160 || y0 < 0 || y1 > 2160 || y0 >= y1 || (!y0 && y1 == 2160))
+        return true;
+
+    // sh_require() is made for an operation that leaves a color behind. This
+    // one leaves nothing: the sampler that follows requires the signature that
+    // the shader had.
+    enum pl_shader_sig signature = sh->output;
+    if (!sh_require(sh, signature, 0, 0))
+        return false;
+    sh->output = signature;
+
+    float bounds[2] = { (float) y0, (float) y1 };
+    if (target && pass->target.planes[0].flipped) {
+        bounds[0] = (float) (2160 - y1);
+        bounds[1] = (float) (2160 - y0);
+    }
+
+    ident_t rows = sh_var(sh, (struct pl_shader_var) {
+        .var     = pl_var_vec2("active_rows"),
+        .data    = bounds,
+        .dynamic = true,
+    });
+
+    if (target) {
+        GLSL("#ifndef PL_ACTIVE_ROWS_TARGET                                  \n"
+             "#error rows of a plane left out by the coordinates of another pass \n"
+             "#endif                                                          \n");
+    }
+
+    GLSL("if (gl_FragCoord.y < "$".x || gl_FragCoord.y >= "$".y) \n"
+         "    return vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);                     \n",
+         rows, rows);
+    return true;
+}
+
 static void dispatch_sampler(struct pass_state *pass, pl_shader sh,
                              struct sampler *sampler, enum sampler_usage usage,
                              pl_tex target_tex, const struct pl_sample_src *src)
 {
     const struct pl_render_params *params = pass->params;
+    // (a plane that is read; `target_tex`: a plane of the target that is written)
+    const bool rows = usage == SAMPLER_PLANE && !target_tex;
+    if (rows && !skip_inactive_rows(pass, sh, src->new_h, true))
+        return;
     if (!sampler)
         goto fallback;
 
@@ -762,6 +810,11 @@
         src2.rect.y1 = src1.new_h;
 
         pl_shader tsh = pl_dispatch_begin(rr->dp);
+        if (rows && !skip_inactive_rows(pass, tsh, src1.new_h, false)) {
+            pl_dispatch_abort(rr->dp, &tsh);
+            ok = false;
+            goto done;
+        }
         ok = pl_shader_sample_ortho2(tsh, &src1, &fparams);
         if (!ok) {
             pl_dispatch_abort(rr->dp, &tsh);
